IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: Part 10 Division 4 Subdivision (5) -- striking a defunct company off the register (ss 344 to 344H).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Part sgm. Text: the SSO informal consolidation as the file renders it (a rendering, not the official text).
-- The rest of Part 10 (ss 247 to 343 and 345 to 354C) is shown repealed (Act 40 of 2018) and has coverage rows only.
--
-- The Registrar's powers and duties are encoded for what they decide and mean to the individual (a director, secretary or member of the company, or a former one):
-- when the name may be struck off, how long there is to show cause, when the company is dissolved, who may ask for the name back and by when, and what an officer must keep.
-- There is no seat for the Registrar, the Court or the Authority; the Registrar's duties are regulative rules (most have no time in the text, so each takes the s 52 input; notes/lest-without-deadline.md).
-- READING A RESULT: JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is the text's no in its own words; NOTHING is "the text does not say".

DECLARE `s 344 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 344(4) publish in the Gazette notice of the striking off of the name of the company`
    `s 344(7)(a) send the particulars to the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore and the Central Provident Fund Board`
    `s 344(7)(b) publish the substance of the notices on the Authority's website`
    `s 344A(3) send the company and its directors, secretaries and members a letter informing them of the application`
    `s 344A(5) strike off the name of the company from the register and publish a notice in the Gazette`
    `s 344A(8)(a) send the particulars of the company and of the application to the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore and the Central Provident Fund Board`
    `s 344A(8)(b) publish the substance of the notices on the Authority's website`
    `s 344B(2)(a) send the company by ordinary post a notice that the application has been withdrawn`
    `s 344B(2)(b) publish a notice on the Authority's website that the application has been withdrawn`
    `s 344C(3)(a) give the applicant or applicants notice of the objection`
    `s 344C(3)(b) take into account the considerations prescribed in deciding whether to allow the objection`
    `s 344E(1) give the applicant notice of the decision`
    `s 344E(2)(b)(i) enter in the register a note of the date on which the restoration takes effect`
    `s 344E(2)(b)(ii) cause notice of the restoration to be published in the Gazette and on the Authority's website`
    `s 344H(1) fail to retain all the books and papers of the company`

§ `Section 344(1) and (1A): the Registrar's letter`

-- "Where the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that a company is not carrying on business or is not in operation, the Registrar may send ... a letter"
-- A grant gated by "Where": ruling (b) of the periods ruling says JUST FALSE when the gate fails and the grant ruling's limit 3 lists the site without changing it (split site (ii); fork F-G5).
-- src:22698 | Power of Registrar to strike defunct company off register
-- src:22700 | 344.—(1) Where the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that
-- src:22701 | a company is not carrying on business or is not in operation, the
-- src:22702 | Registrar may send to the company, and its directors, secretaries and
-- src:22703 | members, a letter to that effect and stating that, if an answer showing
-- src:22704 | cause to the contrary is not received within 30 days after the date of
-- src:22705 | the letter, a notice will be published in the Gazette with a view to
-- src:22706 | striking the name of the company off the register.
@ref s 344(1) (src:22698-22706)
GIVEN `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the company is not carrying on business or is not in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344(1) the Registrar may send the company and its directors, secretaries and members a letter` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the company is not carrying on business or is not in operation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (ii), fork F-G5): "Where the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that a company is not carrying on business or is not in operation, the Registrar may send" -- the "Where" gate of a grant (periods ruling (b): when it fails the answer is JUST FALSE)

-- "if an answer showing cause to the contrary is not received within 30 days after the date of the letter, a notice will be published in the Gazette"
-- src:22700 | 344.—(1) Where the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that
-- src:22701 | a company is not carrying on business or is not in operation, the
-- src:22702 | Registrar may send to the company, and its directors, secretaries and
-- src:22703 | members, a letter to that effect and stating that, if an answer showing
-- src:22704 | cause to the contrary is not received within 30 days after the date of
-- src:22705 | the letter, a notice will be published in the Gazette with a view to
-- src:22706 | striking the name of the company off the register.
@ref s 344(1) (src:22700-22706)
GIVEN `the date of the letter` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 344(1) the last day for an answer showing cause to the contrary` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the letter` 30 Days

-- src:22700 | 344.—(1) Where the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that
-- src:22701 | a company is not carrying on business or is not in operation, the
-- src:22702 | Registrar may send to the company, and its directors, secretaries and
-- src:22703 | members, a letter to that effect and stating that, if an answer showing
-- src:22704 | cause to the contrary is not received within 30 days after the date of
-- src:22705 | the letter, a notice will be published in the Gazette with a view to
-- src:22706 | striking the name of the company off the register.
@ref s 344(1) (src:22700-22706)
GIVEN `the date of the letter` IS A DATE
      `the day on which an answer showing cause to the contrary is received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 344(1) the answer was received within 30 days after the date of the letter` MEANS
    `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of the letter` `the day on which an answer showing cause to the contrary is received` 30 Days

-- (1A): "the Registrar may have regard to such circumstances as may be prescribed" -- a power limited by its own words.
-- src:22710 | (1A) Without limiting subsection (1), in determining whether there
-- src:22711 | is reasonable ground to believe that a company is not carrying on
-- src:22712 | business, the Registrar may have regard to such circumstances as may
-- src:22713 | be prescribed.
@ref s 344(1A) (src:22710-22713)
GIVEN `the circumstance is one prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344(1A) the Registrar may have regard to the circumstance in determining whether the company is not carrying on business` MEANS
    IF `the circumstance is one prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Registrar may have regard to such circumstances as may be prescribed" -- the text says nothing of a circumstance not prescribed (and subsection (1) is "without limiting")

§ `Section 344(2) and (3): the notice that the name will be struck off`

-- (2): "Unless the Registrar receives an answer within one month from the date of the letter to the effect that the company is carrying on business or is in operation,
-- the Registrar may publish in the Gazette and send to the company by registered post a notice that at the expiration of 60 days ... the name of the company ... will ... be struck off"
-- src:22717 | (2) Unless the Registrar receives an answer within one month from
-- src:22718 | the date of the letter to the effect that the company is carrying on
-- src:22719 | business or is in operation, the Registrar may publish in the Gazette
-- src:22720 | and send to the company by registered post a notice that at the
-- src:22721 | expiration of 60 days after the date of that notice the name of the
-- src:22722 | company mentioned in that notice will, unless cause is (in the form
-- src:22723 | and manner specified in section 344C) shown to the contrary, be
-- src:22724 | struck off the register and the company will be dissolved.
@ref s 344(2) (src:22717-22724)
GIVEN `the Registrar has sent the letter mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the letter` IS A DATE
      `an answer to the effect that the company is carrying on business or is in operation has been received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which that answer was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344(2) the Registrar may publish the notice that the name of the company will be struck off` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Registrar has sent the letter mentioned in subsection (1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the power is stated for the company to which the letter was sent ("one month from the date of the letter")
    ELSE (IF `an answer to the effect that the company is carrying on business or is in operation has been received` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of the letter` `the day on which that answer was received` 1 Months
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; fork F-U1): "Unless the Registrar receives an answer within one month from the date of the letter to the effect that the company is carrying on business or is in operation, the Registrar may publish" ("Unless" met)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:22717 | (2) Unless the Registrar receives an answer within one month from
