@ref s 344(3) (src:22728-22748)
GIVEN `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that no liquidator is acting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the affairs of the company are fully wound up and for a period of 6 months the liquidator has been in default in lodging any return required to be made by the liquidator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the affairs of the company have been fully wound up under Division 2 of Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 and there are no assets or the assets available are not sufficient to pay the costs of obtaining an order of the Court dissolving the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344(3) the Registrar may publish in the Gazette and send the notice to the same effect as the notice under subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the company is being wound up` AND (`the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that no liquidator is acting` OR `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the affairs of the company are fully wound up and for a period of 6 months the liquidator has been in default in lodging any return required to be made by the liquidator` OR `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the affairs of the company have been fully wound up under Division 2 of Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 and there are no assets or the assets available are not sufficient to pay the costs of obtaining an order of the Court dissolving the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If in any case where a company is being wound up the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..., the Registrar may publish" (a power whose "If" gate failed; the grant ruling, limit 1; fork F-G1)

§ `Section 344(4) to (6): striking off, dissolution, restoration by the Court`

-- (4): "At the expiration of the time mentioned in the notice, the Registrar may, unless cause to the contrary is previously shown, strike the name of the company off the register"
-- The time mentioned in the notice is the 60 days after its date (subsection (2)); the Registrar may strike off from the day after the 60th.
