      `cause to the contrary has been shown before the time mentioned in the notice expires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344(4) the Registrar may strike the name of the company off the register` MEANS
    IF `cause to the contrary has been shown before the time mentioned in the notice expires`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; fork F-U1): "the Registrar may, unless cause to the contrary is previously shown, strike the name of the company off the register" ("unless" met)
    ELSE (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of the notice` `the date asked` 60 Days
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "At the expiration of the time mentioned in the notice, the Registrar may" (the time has not yet expired; a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); fork F-P5)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

