-- (5): "If any person feels aggrieved by the name of the company having been struck off the register, the Court, on an application made by the person at any time within 6 years
-- after the name of the company has been so struck off may, if satisfied that the company was ... carrying on business or in operation or otherwise that it is just that the name ... be restored, order the name ... to be restored"
-- Outside the 6 years the periods ruling item (a) gives JUST FALSE; within them, the "if satisfied" gate of a grant gives NOTHING when it fails (limit 1 of the grant ruling; fork F-G5, split site (ii)).
