      `the Court is satisfied that otherwise it is just that the name of the company be restored to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344(5) the Court may order the name of the company to be restored to the register` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the day on which the person applies to the Court` AT LEAST `the day on which the name of the company was struck off the register` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day on which the name of the company was struck off the register` `the day on which the person applies to the Court` 6 Years)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on an application made by the person at any time within 6 years after the name of the company has been so struck off" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); fork F-P5)
    ELSE (IF `the person feels aggrieved by the name of the company having been struck off the register` AND (`the Court is satisfied that the company was, at the time of the striking off, carrying on business or in operation` OR `the Court is satisfied that otherwise it is just that the name of the company be restored to the register`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If any person feels aggrieved ..., the Court ... may, if satisfied that ..." (a power whose "If" gate failed; the grant ruling, limit 1; fork F-G5)

