-- src:22791 | company, or, if there is no officer of the company whose name and
-- src:22792 | address are known to the Registrar, may be sent to each of the persons
-- src:22793 | who subscribed the constitution of the company addressed to each
-- src:22794 | person at the address mentioned in the constitution.
@ref s 344(6) (src:22788-22794)
GIVEN `the company has a registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an officer of the company whose name and address are known to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344(6) the letter or notice may be sent to each of the persons who subscribed the constitution` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company has a registered office`) AND (NOT `there is an officer of the company whose name and address are known to the Registrar`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if there is no officer of the company whose name and address are known to the Registrar, may be sent to each of the persons who subscribed the constitution of the company addressed to each person at the address mentioned in the constitution" (a power whose "if" gate failed; the grant ruling, limit 1; fork F-G1)

§ `Section 344(7): what the Registrar must ensure`

-- src:22798 | (7) The Registrar must ensure that —
-- src:22800 | (a) such particulars of the company mentioned in
-- src:22801 | subsection (1) and of the Registrar’s belief that the
-- src:22802 | company is not carrying on business or is not in
-- src:22803 | operation, as the Registrar may determine, is sent to —
-- src:22805 | (i) the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore
-- src:22806 | established under the Inland Revenue Authority of
-- src:22807 | Singapore Act 1992; and
-- src:22809 | (ii) the Central Provident Fund Board established under
-- src:22810 | the Central Provident Fund Act 1953; and
@ref s 344(7)(a) (src:22798-22810)
GIVEN `the company is one mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344(7)(a) the Registrar must ensure that the particulars are sent to the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore and the Central Provident Fund Board` MEANS
    IF `the company is one mentioned in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such particulars of the company mentioned in subsection (1) and of the Registrar's belief that the company is not carrying on business or is not in operation, as the Registrar may determine, is sent to" -- the text names the company mentioned in subsection (1)

-- src:22798 | (7) The Registrar must ensure that —
-- src:22800 | (a) such particulars of the company mentioned in
-- src:22801 | subsection (1) and of the Registrar’s belief that the
-- src:22802 | company is not carrying on business or is not in
-- src:22803 | operation, as the Registrar may determine, is sent to —
-- src:22805 | (i) the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore
-- src:22806 | established under the Inland Revenue Authority of
-- src:22807 | Singapore Act 1992; and
-- src:22809 | (ii) the Central Provident Fund Board established under
-- src:22810 | the Central Provident Fund Act 1953; and
@ref s 344(7)(a) (src:22798-22810)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 344 act`
`s 344(7)(a) the Registrar must send the particulars to the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore and the Central Provident Fund Board (rule)` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 344(7)(a) send the particulars to the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore and the Central Provident Fund Board`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not ensure that the particulars were sent to the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore and the Central Provident Fund Board"

-- src:22798 | (7) The Registrar must ensure that —
-- src:22812 | (b) the substance of the notices to be published in the Gazette
-- src:22813 | referred to in subsections (2), (3) and (4) is also published
-- src:22814 | on the Authority’s website.
@ref s 344(7)(b) (src:22798-22814)
GIVEN `the notice is one to be published in the Gazette under subsection (2), (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344(7)(b) the Registrar must ensure that the substance of the notice is also published on the Authority's website` MEANS
    IF `the notice is one to be published in the Gazette under subsection (2), (3) or (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the substance of the notices to be published in the Gazette referred to in subsections (2), (3) and (4) is also published on the Authority's website" -- the text names those notices

-- src:22798 | (7) The Registrar must ensure that —
-- src:22812 | (b) the substance of the notices to be published in the Gazette
-- src:22813 | referred to in subsections (2), (3) and (4) is also published
-- src:22814 | on the Authority’s website.
@ref s 344(7)(b) (src:22798-22814)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 344 act`
`s 344(7)(b) the Registrar must publish the substance of the notices on the Authority's website (rule)` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 344(7)(b) publish the substance of the notices on the Authority's website`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not ensure that the substance of the notices was also published on the Authority's website"

§ `Section 344A: striking off on application by the company`

-- (1): "The Registrar may, on the application by a company, strike the company's name off the register on such grounds and subject to such conditions as may be prescribed."
-- src:22818 | Striking off on application by company
-- src:22820 | 344A.—(1) The Registrar may, on the application by a company,
-- src:22821 | strike the company’s name off the register on such grounds and
-- src:22822 | subject to such conditions as may be prescribed.
@ref s 344A(1) (src:22818-22822)
GIVEN `the company has applied to the Registrar to strike its name off the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grounds prescribed are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions prescribed (if any) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344A(1) the Registrar may strike the company's name off the register on the application of the company` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company has applied to the Registrar to strike its name off the register`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (ii), fork F-G5): "The Registrar may, on the application by a company, strike the company's name off the register" -- an "on the application" (upon) gate: "upon" counts as "where" (delegated-definitions ruling (c); periods ruling (b)); the grant ruling's limit 3 lists the site and does not change it
    ELSE (IF `the grounds prescribed are satisfied` AND `the conditions prescribed (if any) are satisfied`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on such grounds and subject to such conditions as may be prescribed" (a power limited by its own wording to the prescribed grounds and conditions; fork F-G5)

-- src:22826 | (2) An application under subsection (1) is to be made on the
-- src:22827 | company’s behalf by its directors or by a majority of them.
@ref s 344A(2) (src:22826-22827)
GIVEN `the application is made on the company's behalf by all its directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made on the company's behalf by a majority of its directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344A(2) the application is made on the company's behalf as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the application is made on the company's behalf by all its directors` OR `the application is made on the company's behalf by a majority of its directors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application under subsection (1) is to be made on the company's behalf by its directors or by a majority of them" (a requirement not met)

-- (3): "Upon receipt of the application, the Registrar must, if satisfied that the grounds and conditions (if any) ... have been satisfied, send to the company and its directors, secretaries and members a letter"
-- src:22834 | (3) Upon receipt of the application, the Registrar must, if satisfied
-- src:22835 | that the grounds and conditions (if any) referred to in subsection (1)
-- src:22836 | have been satisfied, send to the company and its directors, secretaries
-- src:22837 | and members a letter informing them of the application and stating
-- src:22838 | that if an answer showing cause to the contrary (in the form and
-- src:22839 | manner referred to in section 344C) is not received within 30 days
-- src:22840 | after the date thereof a notice, details of which are set out in
-- src:22841 | subsection (4), will be published in the Gazette with a view to striking
-- src:22842 | the name of the company off the register.
@ref s 344A(3) (src:22834-22842)
GIVEN `the Registrar has received the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the grounds and conditions (if any) have been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344A(3) the Registrar must send the company and its directors, secretaries and members a letter informing them of the application` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has received the application` AND `the Registrar is satisfied that the grounds and conditions (if any) have been satisfied`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; fork F-W1): "Upon receipt of the application, the Registrar must, if satisfied that the grounds and conditions (if any) ... have been satisfied, send" ("Upon" counts as "where", delegated-definitions ruling (c); the "if" gate of a duty)

-- src:22834 | (3) Upon receipt of the application, the Registrar must, if satisfied
-- src:22835 | that the grounds and conditions (if any) referred to in subsection (1)
-- src:22836 | have been satisfied, send to the company and its directors, secretaries
-- src:22837 | and members a letter informing them of the application and stating
-- src:22838 | that if an answer showing cause to the contrary (in the form and
-- src:22839 | manner referred to in section 344C) is not received within 30 days
-- src:22840 | after the date thereof a notice, details of which are set out in
-- src:22841 | subsection (4), will be published in the Gazette with a view to striking
-- src:22842 | the name of the company off the register.
@ref s 344A(3) (src:22834-22842)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 344 act`
`s 344A(3) the Registrar must send the letter informing the company, its directors, secretaries and members of the application (rule)` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 344A(3) send the company and its directors, secretaries and members a letter informing them of the application`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not send the company and its directors, secretaries and members a letter informing them of the application"

-- src:22834 | (3) Upon receipt of the application, the Registrar must, if satisfied
-- src:22835 | that the grounds and conditions (if any) referred to in subsection (1)
-- src:22836 | have been satisfied, send to the company and its directors, secretaries
-- src:22837 | and members a letter informing them of the application and stating
-- src:22838 | that if an answer showing cause to the contrary (in the form and
-- src:22839 | manner referred to in section 344C) is not received within 30 days
-- src:22840 | after the date thereof a notice, details of which are set out in
-- src:22841 | subsection (4), will be published in the Gazette with a view to striking
-- src:22842 | the name of the company off the register.
@ref s 344A(3) (src:22834-22842)
GIVEN `the date of the letter` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 344A(3) the last day for an answer showing cause to the contrary` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the letter` 30 Days

-- (4): "The Registrar may not strike a company's name off the register under this section until after the expiration of 60 days after the publication by the Registrar in the Gazette
-- of a notice (a) stating that the Registrar intends to exercise the power ...; and (b) inviting any person to show cause why that should not be done within such period as may be prescribed."
-- The "until" bar (delegated-definitions ruling (d)): JUST TRUE (barred) until the 60 days have run, JUST FALSE after. With no such notice published the 60 days have not begun and the bar stands.
-- src:22846 | (4) The Registrar may not strike a company’s name off the register
-- src:22847 | under this section until after the expiration of 60 days after the
-- src:22848 | publication by the Registrar in the Gazette of a notice —
-- src:22850 | (a) stating that the Registrar intends to exercise the power
-- src:22851 | under this section in relation to the company; and
-- src:22853 | (b) inviting any person to show cause why that should not be
-- src:22854 | done within such period as may be prescribed.
@ref s 344A(4) (src:22846-22854)
GIVEN `the Registrar has published in the Gazette a notice stating that the Registrar intends to exercise the power under section 344A in relation to the company and inviting any person to show cause why that should not be done within the period prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which that notice was published` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344A(4) the Registrar is barred from striking the company's name off the register under this section` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Registrar has published in the Gazette a notice stating that the Registrar intends to exercise the power under section 344A in relation to the company and inviting any person to show cause why that should not be done within the period prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day on which that notice was published` `the date asked` 60 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; delegated-definitions ruling (d)): "may not strike a company's name off the register under this section until after the expiration of 60 days after the publication ... of a notice" (after the expiration the bar no longer holds)

-- src:22846 | (4) The Registrar may not strike a company’s name off the register
-- src:22847 | under this section until after the expiration of 60 days after the
-- src:22848 | publication by the Registrar in the Gazette of a notice —
-- src:22850 | (a) stating that the Registrar intends to exercise the power
-- src:22851 | under this section in relation to the company; and
-- src:22853 | (b) inviting any person to show cause why that should not be
-- src:22854 | done within such period as may be prescribed.
@ref s 344A(4) (src:22846-22854)
GIVEN `the day on which that notice was published` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 344A(4) the last day of the 60 days after the publication of the notice` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day on which that notice was published` 60 Days

-- (5): "If no person shows cause or sufficient cause within the period referred to in subsection (4)(b) ..., the Registrar must strike off the name of the company from the register and publish a notice in the Gazette"
-- src:22858 | (5) If no person shows cause or sufficient cause within the period
-- src:22859 | referred to in subsection (4)(b) as to why the name of the company
-- src:22860 | should not be struck off the register, the Registrar must strike off the
-- src:22861 | name of the company from the register and publish a notice in the
-- src:22862 | Gazette of the company’s name having been so struck off.
@ref s 344A(5) (src:22858-22862)
GIVEN `no person has shown cause or sufficient cause within the period referred to in subsection (4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344A(5) the Registrar must strike off the name of the company from the register and publish a notice in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF `no person has shown cause or sufficient cause within the period referred to in subsection (4)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; fork F-W1): "If no person shows cause or sufficient cause within the period referred to in subsection (4)(b) as to why the name of the company should not be struck off the register, the Registrar must strike off the name" (the "If" gate of a duty)

-- src:22858 | (5) If no person shows cause or sufficient cause within the period
-- src:22859 | referred to in subsection (4)(b) as to why the name of the company
-- src:22860 | should not be struck off the register, the Registrar must strike off the
-- src:22861 | name of the company from the register and publish a notice in the
-- src:22862 | Gazette of the company’s name having been so struck off.
@ref s 344A(5) (src:22858-22862)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 344 act`
`s 344A(5) the Registrar must strike off the name of the company from the register and publish a notice in the Gazette (rule)` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 344A(5) strike off the name of the company from the register and publish a notice in the Gazette`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not strike off the name of the company from the register and publish a notice in the Gazette"

-- src:22866 | (6) On the publication of the notice in the Gazette under
-- src:22867 | subsection (5), the company is dissolved.
@ref s 344A(6) (src:22866-22867)
GIVEN `the Registrar has published in the Gazette the notice under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344A(6) the company is dissolved` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has published in the Gazette the notice under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the publication of the notice in the Gazette under subsection (5), the company is dissolved" -- the text says nothing of a company the notice has not been published for

-- src:22871 | (7) Despite the dissolution of the company under subsection (6) —
-- src:22873 | (a) the liability (if any) of every officer and member of the
-- src:22874 | company continues and may be enforced as if the company
-- src:22875 | had not been dissolved; and
@ref s 344A(7)(a) (src:22871-22875)
GIVEN `the company has been dissolved under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer or a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344A(7)(a) the liability of the officer or member continues and may be enforced as if the company had not been dissolved` MEANS
    IF `the company has been dissolved under subsection (6)` AND `the person is an officer or a member of the company` AND `the person has a liability`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Despite the dissolution of the company under subsection (6) -- (a) the liability (if any) of every officer and member of the company continues" -- the text says nothing of a person with no liability, of a person who is neither officer nor member, or of a company not dissolved under subsection (6)

-- src:22871 | (7) Despite the dissolution of the company under subsection (6) —
-- src:22877 | (b) nothing in this section affects the power of the Court to
-- src:22878 | wind up a company the name of which has been struck off
-- src:22879 | the register.
@ref s 344A(7)(b) (src:22871-22879)
GIVEN `the name of the company has been struck off the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344A(7)(b) the Court may wind up the company the name of which has been struck off the register` MEANS
    IF `the name of the company has been struck off the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "nothing in this section affects the power of the Court to wind up a company the name of which has been struck off the register" -- the text speaks of a company whose name has been struck off

-- src:22886 | (8) The Registrar must ensure that —
-- src:22888 | (a) such particulars of the company and of the application
-- src:22889 | mentioned in subsection (1), as the Registrar may
-- src:22890 | determine, is sent to —
-- src:22892 | (i) the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore
