§ `Sections 344B and 344C: withdrawal and objections`

-- 344B(1): "The applicant or applicants may, by written notice to the Registrar, withdraw an application ... at any time before the name of the company has been struck off the register."
-- src:22910 | Withdrawal of application
-- src:22912 | 344B.—(1) The applicant or applicants may, by written notice to
-- src:22913 | the Registrar, withdraw an application to strike a company’s name off
-- src:22914 | the register under section 344A at any time before the name of the
-- src:22915 | company has been struck off the register.
@ref s 344B(1) (src:22910-22915)
GIVEN `the applicant gives the Registrar written notice of the withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name of the company has been struck off the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344B(1) the applicant may withdraw the application to strike the company's name off the register` MEANS
    IF `the name of the company has been struck off the register`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time before the name of the company has been struck off the register" (a period the text fixes in its own words; after the striking off the periods ruling item (a) gives JUST FALSE; fork F-P5)
    ELSE (IF `the applicant gives the Registrar written notice of the withdrawal`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The applicant or applicants may, by written notice to the Registrar, withdraw" (a power gated by the manner of withdrawing; the text says nothing of a withdrawal not by written notice; fork F-G1)

-- src:22919 | (2) Upon receipt of the notice mentioned in subsection (1), the
-- src:22920 | Registrar must —
-- src:22922 | (a) send to the company by ordinary post a notice that the
-- src:22923 | application to strike the company’s name off the register
-- src:22924 | has been withdrawn; and
@ref s 344B(2)(a) (src:22919-22924)
GIVEN `the Registrar has received the notice mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344B(2)(a) the Registrar must send the company by ordinary post a notice that the application has been withdrawn` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has received the notice mentioned in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; fork F-W1): "Upon receipt of the notice mentioned in subsection (1), the Registrar must (a) send to the company by ordinary post a notice" ("Upon" counts as "where", delegated-definitions ruling (c))

-- src:22919 | (2) Upon receipt of the notice mentioned in subsection (1), the
-- src:22920 | Registrar must —
-- src:22926 | (b) publish a notice on the Authority’s website that the
-- src:22927 | application to strike the company’s name off the register
-- src:22928 | has been withdrawn.
@ref s 344B(2)(b) (src:22919-22928)
GIVEN `the Registrar has received the notice mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344B(2)(b) the Registrar must publish a notice on the Authority's website that the application has been withdrawn` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has received the notice mentioned in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; fork F-W1): "Upon receipt of the notice mentioned in subsection (1), the Registrar must (b) publish a notice on the Authority's website" ("Upon" counts as "where", delegated-definitions ruling (c))

-- src:22919 | (2) Upon receipt of the notice mentioned in subsection (1), the
-- src:22920 | Registrar must —
-- src:22922 | (a) send to the company by ordinary post a notice that the
-- src:22923 | application to strike the company’s name off the register
-- src:22924 | has been withdrawn; and
@ref s 344B(2)(a) (src:22919-22924)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 344 act`
`s 344B(2)(a) the Registrar must send the company a notice that the application has been withdrawn (rule)` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 344B(2)(a) send the company by ordinary post a notice that the application has been withdrawn`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not send the company by ordinary post a notice that the application has been withdrawn"

-- src:22919 | (2) Upon receipt of the notice mentioned in subsection (1), the
-- src:22920 | Registrar must —
-- src:22926 | (b) publish a notice on the Authority’s website that the
-- src:22927 | application to strike the company’s name off the register
-- src:22928 | has been withdrawn.
@ref s 344B(2)(b) (src:22919-22928)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 344 act`
`s 344B(2)(b) the Registrar must publish a notice on the Authority's website that the application has been withdrawn (rule)` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 344B(2)(b) publish a notice on the Authority's website that the application has been withdrawn`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not publish a notice on the Authority's website that the application has been withdrawn"

-- 344C(1): "Where a notice is given or published ... under section 344(2) or 344A(4) of the Registrar's intention to strike the company's name off the register, any person may deliver, not later than
-- the date specified in the notice, an objection ... on the ground that there is reasonable cause why the name of the company should not be so struck off"
-- src:22932 | Objections to striking off
-- src:22934 | 344C.—(1) Where a notice is given or published by the Registrar
-- src:22935 | under section 344(2) or 344A(4) of the Registrar’s intention to strike
-- src:22940 | the company’s name off the register, any person may deliver, not later
-- src:22941 | than the date specified in the notice, an objection to the striking off of
-- src:22942 | the name of the company from the register on the ground that there is
-- src:22943 | reasonable cause why the name of the company should not be so
-- src:22944 | struck off, including that the company does not satisfy any of the
-- src:22945 | prescribed grounds for striking off referred to in section 344(1) or
-- src:22946 | 344A(1).
@ref s 344C(1) (src:22932-22946)
GIVEN `a notice of the Registrar's intention to strike the company's name off the register has been given or published under section 344(2) or 344A(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date specified in the notice` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the objection is delivered` IS A DATE
      `the objection is made on the ground that there is reasonable cause why the name of the company should not be struck off` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344C(1) any person may deliver an objection to the striking off of the name of the company` MEANS
    IF NOT `a notice of the Registrar's intention to strike the company's name off the register has been given or published under section 344(2) or 344A(4)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (ii), fork F-G5): "Where a notice is given or published by the Registrar under section 344(2) or 344A(4) ..., any person may deliver ... an objection" -- the "Where" gate of a grant (periods ruling (b))
    ELSE (IF `the day on which the objection is delivered` GREATER THAN `the date specified in the notice`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than the date specified in the notice" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); fork F-P5)
          ELSE (IF `the objection is made on the ground that there is reasonable cause why the name of the company should not be struck off`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an objection ... on the ground that there is reasonable cause why the name of the company should not be so struck off" (a power limited by its own wording; fork F-G1)

-- src:22950 | (2) An objection to the striking the name of the company off the
-- src:22951 | register mentioned in subsection (1) must be given to the Registrar by
-- src:22952 | notice in the prescribed form and manner.
@ref s 344C(2) (src:22950-22952)
GIVEN `the objection is given to the Registrar by notice in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344C(2) the objection is given as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the objection is given to the Registrar by notice in the prescribed form and manner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An objection ... must be given to the Registrar by notice in the prescribed form and manner" (a requirement not met)

-- src:22956 | (3) Upon receipt of a notice of objection, which is made in the
-- src:22957 | prescribed form and manner, within the time referred to in
-- src:22958 | subsection (1), the Registrar —
-- src:22960 | (a) must where applicable, give the applicant or applicants for
-- src:22961 | striking the name of the company off the register notice of
-- src:22962 | the objection; and
@ref s 344C(3)(a) (src:22956-22962)
GIVEN `the Registrar has received a notice of objection, made in the prescribed form and manner, within the time referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are applicants for striking the name of the company off the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344C(3)(a) the Registrar must give the applicant or applicants notice of the objection` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has received a notice of objection, made in the prescribed form and manner, within the time referred to in subsection (1)` AND `there are applicants for striking the name of the company off the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; fork F-W1): "Upon receipt of a notice of objection ..., the Registrar (a) must where applicable, give the applicant or applicants ... notice of the objection" ("Upon" and "where applicable" are "where" gates of a duty, delegated-definitions ruling (c))

-- src:22956 | (3) Upon receipt of a notice of objection, which is made in the
-- src:22957 | prescribed form and manner, within the time referred to in
-- src:22958 | subsection (1), the Registrar —
-- src:22964 | (b) must, in deciding whether to allow the objection, take into
-- src:22965 | account such considerations as may be prescribed.
@ref s 344C(3)(b) (src:22956-22965)
GIVEN `the Registrar has received a notice of objection, made in the prescribed form and manner, within the time referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344C(3)(b) the Registrar must take into account the considerations prescribed in deciding whether to allow the objection` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has received a notice of objection, made in the prescribed form and manner, within the time referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; fork F-W1): "Upon receipt of a notice of objection ..., the Registrar ... (b) must, in deciding whether to allow the objection, take into account such considerations as may be prescribed" ("Upon" counts as "where", delegated-definitions ruling (c))

-- src:22956 | (3) Upon receipt of a notice of objection, which is made in the
-- src:22957 | prescribed form and manner, within the time referred to in
-- src:22958 | subsection (1), the Registrar —
-- src:22960 | (a) must where applicable, give the applicant or applicants for
-- src:22961 | striking the name of the company off the register notice of
-- src:22962 | the objection; and
@ref s 344C(3)(a) (src:22956-22962)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 344 act`
`s 344C(3)(a) the Registrar must give the applicant or applicants notice of the objection (rule)` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 344C(3)(a) give the applicant or applicants notice of the objection`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not give the applicant or applicants notice of the objection"

-- src:22956 | (3) Upon receipt of a notice of objection, which is made in the
-- src:22957 | prescribed form and manner, within the time referred to in
-- src:22958 | subsection (1), the Registrar —
-- src:22964 | (b) must, in deciding whether to allow the objection, take into
-- src:22965 | account such considerations as may be prescribed.
@ref s 344C(3)(b) (src:22956-22965)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 344 act`
`s 344C(3)(b) the Registrar must take into account the prescribed considerations (rule)` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 344C(3)(b) take into account the considerations prescribed in deciding whether to allow the objection`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 344C(3)(b) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not take into account the considerations prescribed in deciding whether to allow the objection" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

§ `Sections 344D to 344F: restoring the name`

-- 344D(1): "Subject to such conditions as may be prescribed, an application may be made to the Registrar to restore to the register the name of a company whose name has been struck off the register
-- by the Registrar under section 344, if no application has been or is being made to the Court to restore the name of the company to the register under section 344(5)."
-- src:22971 | 344D.—(1) Subject to such conditions as may be prescribed, an
-- src:22972 | application may be made to the Registrar to restore to the register the
-- src:22973 | name of a company whose name has been struck off the register by
-- src:22974 | the Registrar under section 344, if no application has been or is being
-- src:22975 | made to the Court to restore the name of the company to the register
-- src:22976 | under section 344(5).
@ref s 344D(1) (src:22971-22976)
GIVEN `the name of the company was struck off the register by the Registrar under section 344` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no application has been or is being made to the Court to restore the name of the company under section 344(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions prescribed (if any) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344D(1) an application may be made to the Registrar to restore the name of the company to the register` MEANS
    IF `the name of the company was struck off the register by the Registrar under section 344` AND `no application has been or is being made to the Court to restore the name of the company under section 344(5)` AND `the conditions prescribed (if any) are satisfied`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an application may be made to the Registrar to restore ... the name of a company whose name has been struck off the register by the Registrar under section 344, if no application has been or is being made to the Court" (a power whose "if" gate failed; the grant ruling, limit 1; fork F-G1). A name struck off under section 344A is not within this subsection; section 344F is the route for a mistake.

-- src:22980 | (2) An application under this section may be made whether or not
-- src:22981 | the company has in consequence been dissolved.
@ref s 344D(2) (src:22980-22981)
GIVEN `the company has in consequence been dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344D(2) the application may be made whether or not the company has in consequence been dissolved` MEANS
    IF `the company has in consequence been dissolved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST TRUE   -- the same answer on both facts: "An application under this section may be made whether or not the company has in consequence been dissolved"

-- src:22985 | (3) An application under this section may only be made by a former
-- src:22986 | director or former member of the company.
@ref s 344D(3) (src:22985-22986)
GIVEN `the person is a former director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a former member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344D(3) the person may make the application` MEANS
    IF `the person is a former director of the company` OR `the person is a former member of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application under this section may only be made by a former director or former member of the company" (list closed with "only")

-- (4): "An application ... is not valid unless the application is received by the Registrar within 6 years after the date on which the company is dissolved."
-- An application received before the dissolution (subsection (2) allows one) is read as valid: the 6 years are an upper limit (finding 3 in NOTES.md).
-- src:22993 | (4) An application under this section is not valid unless the
-- src:22994 | application is received by the Registrar within 6 years after the
-- src:22995 | date on which the company is dissolved.
@ref s 344D(4) (src:22993-22995)
GIVEN `the day on which the Registrar receives the application` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company is dissolved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344D(4) the application is valid as to time` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the Registrar receives the application` AT MOST `period: the last day of a period after` `the date on which the company is dissolved` 6 Years
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application under this section is not valid unless the application is received by the Registrar within 6 years after the date on which the company is dissolved" ("unless" not met; fork F-P5)

-- src:22999 | Registrar’s decision on application for administrative
-- src:23000 | restoration
-- src:23002 | 344E.—(1) The Registrar must give notice to the applicant of the
-- src:23003 | decision on an application under section 344D.
@ref s 344E(1) (src:22999-23003)
GIVEN `the Registrar has made a decision on an application under section 344D` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344E(1) the Registrar must give the applicant notice of the decision` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has made a decision on an application under section 344D`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the duty follows the decision; before a decision the text says nothing (fork F-E1)

-- src:22999 | Registrar’s decision on application for administrative
-- src:23000 | restoration
-- src:23002 | 344E.—(1) The Registrar must give notice to the applicant of the
-- src:23003 | decision on an application under section 344D.
@ref s 344E(1) (src:22999-23003)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 344 act`
`s 344E(1) the Registrar must give the applicant notice of the decision (rule)` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 344E(1) give the applicant notice of the decision`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not give the applicant notice of the decision on the application"

-- (2)(a): "If the Registrar's decision is that the name of the company should be restored to the register -- (a) the restoration takes effect as from the date that notice is sent"
-- src:23007 | (2) If the Registrar’s decision is that the name of the company
-- src:23008 | should be restored to the register —
-- src:23010 | (a) the restoration takes effect as from the date that notice is
-- src:23011 | sent; and
@ref s 344E(2)(a) (src:23007-23011)
GIVEN `the Registrar's decision is that the name of the company should be restored to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the notice of the decision is sent` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344E(2)(a) the restoration has taken effect` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Registrar's decision is that the name of the company should be restored to the register`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Registrar's decision is that the name of the company should be restored to the register" -- the text says nothing of a decision not to restore
    ELSE (IF `the date asked` AT LEAST `the date on which the notice of the decision is sent`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the restoration takes effect as from the date that notice is sent" (a period the text fixes in its own words; before it the periods ruling item (a) gives JUST FALSE; fork F-P5)

-- src:23007 | (2) If the Registrar’s decision is that the name of the company
-- src:23008 | should be restored to the register —
-- src:23013 | (b) the Registrar must —
-- src:23015 | (i) enter in the register a note of the date on which the
-- src:23016 | restoration takes effect; and
@ref s 344E(2)(b)(i) (src:23007-23016)
GIVEN `the Registrar's decision is that the name of the company should be restored to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344E(2)(b)(i) the Registrar must enter in the register a note of the date on which the restoration takes effect` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar's decision is that the name of the company should be restored to the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; fork F-W1): "If the Registrar's decision is that the name of the company should be restored to the register ... the Registrar must (i) enter in the register a note of the date on which the restoration takes effect" (the "If" gate of a duty)

-- src:23007 | (2) If the Registrar’s decision is that the name of the company
-- src:23008 | should be restored to the register —
-- src:23013 | (b) the Registrar must —
-- src:23018 | (ii) cause notice of the restoration to be published in the
-- src:23019 | Gazette and on the Authority’s website.
@ref s 344E(2)(b)(ii) (src:23007-23019)
GIVEN `the Registrar's decision is that the name of the company should be restored to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344E(2)(b)(ii) the Registrar must cause notice of the restoration to be published in the Gazette and on the Authority's website` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar's decision is that the name of the company should be restored to the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; fork F-W1): "If the Registrar's decision is that the name of the company should be restored to the register ... the Registrar must (ii) cause notice of the restoration to be published in the Gazette and on the Authority's website" (the "If" gate of a duty)

-- src:23007 | (2) If the Registrar’s decision is that the name of the company
-- src:23008 | should be restored to the register —
-- src:23013 | (b) the Registrar must —
-- src:23015 | (i) enter in the register a note of the date on which the
-- src:23016 | restoration takes effect; and
@ref s 344E(2)(b)(i) (src:23007-23016)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 344 act`
`s 344E(2)(b)(i) the Registrar must enter in the register a note of the date of the restoration (rule)` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 344E(2)(b)(i) enter in the register a note of the date on which the restoration takes effect`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not enter in the register a note of the date on which the restoration takes effect"

-- src:23007 | (2) If the Registrar’s decision is that the name of the company
-- src:23008 | should be restored to the register —
-- src:23013 | (b) the Registrar must —
-- src:23018 | (ii) cause notice of the restoration to be published in the
-- src:23019 | Gazette and on the Authority’s website.
@ref s 344E(2)(b)(ii) (src:23007-23019)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 344 act`
`s 344E(2)(b)(ii) the Registrar must cause notice of the restoration to be published (rule)` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 344E(2)(b)(ii) cause notice of the restoration to be published in the Gazette and on the Authority's website`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not cause notice of the restoration to be published in the Gazette and on the Authority's website"

-- (3): the notice must state (a) the name (and the former name if restored under a different name); (b) the registration number; (c) the date the restoration takes effect.
-- src:23023 | (3) The notice under subsection (2)(b)(ii) must state —
-- src:23025 | (a) the name of the company or, if the company is restored to
-- src:23026 | the register under a different name, that name and its
-- src:23027 | former name;
-- src:23029 | (b) the company’s registration number; and
-- src:23031 | (c) the date as on which the restoration of the name of the
-- src:23032 | company to the register takes effect.
@ref s 344E(3) (src:23023-23032)
GIVEN `the company is restored to the register under a different name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the name of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the former name of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the company's registration number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the date as on which the restoration takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344E(3) the notice states what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF     `the notice states the name of the company`
       AND ((NOT `the company is restored to the register under a different name`) OR `the notice states the former name of the company`)
       AND `the notice states the company's registration number`
       AND `the notice states the date as on which the restoration takes effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice under subsection (2)(b)(ii) must state (a) the name of the company or, if the company is restored to the register under a different name, that name and its former name; (b) the company's registration number; and (c) the date ..." (a requirement not met)

-- (4): "If the Registrar's decision is that the name of the company should not be restored to the register, the person who made the application ... or any other person aggrieved by the decision ... may appeal to the Court."
-- src:23036 | (4) If the Registrar’s decision is that the name of the company
-- src:23037 | should not be restored to the register, the person who made the
-- src:23038 | application under section 344D or any other person aggrieved by the
-- src:23039 | decision of the Registrar may appeal to the Court.
@ref s 344E(4) (src:23036-23039)
GIVEN `the Registrar's decision is that the name of the company should not be restored to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made the application under section 344D` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is aggrieved by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344E(4) the person may appeal to the Court` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar's decision is that the name of the company should not be restored to the register` AND (`the person made the application under section 344D` OR `the person is aggrieved by the decision`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Registrar's decision is that the name of the company should not be restored ..., the person who made the application ... or any other person aggrieved by the decision ... may appeal to the Court" (a power whose "If" gate failed; the grant ruling, limit 1; fork F-G1)

-- src:23043 | (5) On an appeal made under subsection (4), the Court may —
-- src:23045 | (a) confirm the Registrar’s decision; or
@ref s 344E(5)(a) (src:23043-23045)
GIVEN `an appeal has been made under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344E(5)(a) the Court may confirm the Registrar's decision` MEANS
    IF `an appeal has been made under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (ii), fork F-G5): "On an appeal made under subsection (4), the Court may (a) confirm the Registrar's decision" -- an "On" (upon) gate of a power: "upon" counts as "where" (delegated-definitions ruling (c); periods ruling (b)); the grant ruling's limit 3 lists the site and does not change it

-- src:23043 | (5) On an appeal made under subsection (4), the Court may —
-- src:23050 | (b) restore the name of the company to the register and give
-- src:23051 | such directions and make such orders as the Court is
-- src:23052 | empowered to give and make under section 344G(3).
@ref s 344E(5)(b) (src:23043-23052)
GIVEN `an appeal has been made under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344E(5)(b) the Court may restore the name of the company to the register and give directions and make orders` MEANS
    IF `an appeal has been made under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (ii), fork F-G5): "On an appeal made under subsection (4), the Court may ... (b) restore the name of the company to the register and give such directions and make such orders as the Court is empowered to give and make under section 344G(3)" -- an "On" (upon) gate of a power: "upon" counts as "where" (delegated-definitions ruling (c); periods ruling (b)); the grant ruling's limit 3 lists the site and does not change it

-- 344F(1) and (2): "The Registrar may, on his or her own initiative, restore the name ... if the Registrar is satisfied that the name ... has been struck off ... and the company is dissolved under section 344 or 344A
-- as a result of a mistake of the Registrar." A mistake of the Registrar "excludes a mistake that is made on the basis of wrong, false or misleading information given by the applicant".
-- src:23066 | (2) In subsection (1), a reference to a mistake of the Registrar
-- src:23067 | excludes a mistake that is made on the basis of wrong, false or
-- src:23068 | misleading information given by the applicant in connection with the
-- src:23069 | application for striking the name of the company off the register
-- src:23070 | under section 344A.
@ref s 344F(2) (src:23066-23070)
GIVEN `the name of the company has been struck off the register and the company dissolved as a result of a mistake` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mistake was made on the basis of wrong, false or misleading information given by the applicant in connection with the application under section 344A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344F(2) the mistake is a mistake of the Registrar` MEANS
    IF NOT `the name of the company has been struck off the register and the company dissolved as a result of a mistake`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection explains "a mistake of the Registrar" and says nothing where there was no mistake
    ELSE (IF `the mistake was made on the basis of wrong, false or misleading information given by the applicant in connection with the application under section 344A`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference to a mistake of the Registrar excludes a mistake that is made on the basis of wrong, false or misleading information given by the applicant"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:23056 | Registrar may restore company deregistered by mistake
-- src:23058 | 344F.—(1) The Registrar may, on his or her own initiative, restore
-- src:23059 | the name of a company to the register if the Registrar is satisfied that
-- src:23060 | the name of the company has been struck off the register and the
-- src:23061 | company is dissolved under section 344 or 344A as a result of a
-- src:23062 | mistake of the Registrar.
@ref s 344F(1) (src:23056-23062)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the name of the company has been struck off the register and the company is dissolved under section 344 or 344A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name of the company has been struck off the register and the company dissolved as a result of a mistake` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mistake was made on the basis of wrong, false or misleading information given by the applicant in connection with the application under section 344A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344F(1) the Registrar may on his or her own initiative restore the name of the company to the register` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is satisfied that the name of the company has been struck off the register and the company is dissolved under section 344 or 344A` AND `s 344F(2) the mistake is a mistake of the Registrar` `the name of the company has been struck off the register and the company dissolved as a result of a mistake` `the mistake was made on the basis of wrong, false or misleading information given by the applicant in connection with the application under section 344A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registrar may, on his or her own initiative, restore the name of a company to the register if the Registrar is satisfied that ..." (a power whose "if" gate failed; the grant ruling, limit 1; fork F-G1)

-- src:23074 | (3) The Registrar may restore the name of a company to the register
-- src:23075 | by publishing in the Gazette and on the Authority’s website a notice
-- src:23076 | declaring the restoration, and the restoration takes effect on the date
-- src:23077 | of publication of the notice.
@ref s 344F(3) (src:23074-23077)
GIVEN `the Registrar has published in the Gazette and on the Authority's website a notice declaring the restoration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of publication of the notice` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344F(3) the restoration has taken effect` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Registrar has published in the Gazette and on the Authority's website a notice declaring the restoration`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Registrar may restore the name ... by publishing in the Gazette and on the Authority's website a notice declaring the restoration" -- the text says nothing of a restoration not so made
    ELSE (IF `the date asked` AT LEAST `the date of publication of the notice`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the restoration takes effect on the date of publication of the notice" (before it the periods ruling item (a) gives JUST FALSE; fork F-P5)

§ `Sections 344G and 344H: the effect of restoration; books and papers`

-- src:23083 | 344G.—(1) If the name of a company is restored to the register
-- src:23084 | under section 344E(2) or 344F, or on appeal to the Court under
-- src:23085 | section 344E(5), the company is to be regarded as having continued
-- src:23086 | in existence as if its name had not been struck off the register.
@ref s 344G(1) (src:23083-23086)
GIVEN `the name of the company is restored to the register under section 344E(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name of the company is restored to the register under section 344F` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name of the company is restored to the register on appeal to the Court under section 344E(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344G(1) the company is regarded as having continued in existence as if its name had not been struck off the register` MEANS
    IF `the name of the company is restored to the register under section 344E(2)` OR `the name of the company is restored to the register under section 344F` OR `the name of the company is restored to the register on appeal to the Court under section 344E(5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the name of a company is restored to the register under section 344E(2) or 344F, or on appeal to the Court under section 344E(5), the company is to be regarded as having continued in existence" -- the text says nothing of a restoration by the Court under section 344(5), which has its own deeming rule

-- src:23090 | (2) The company and its directors are not liable to a penalty under
-- src:23091 | section 204 for a financial year in relation to which the period for
-- src:23092 | filing its financial statements and other related statements ended —
-- src:23094 | (a) after the date of dissolution or striking off; and
-- src:23096 | (b) before the restoration of the name of the company to the
-- src:23097 | register.
@ref s 344G(2) (src:23090-23097)
GIVEN `the day on which the period for filing the financial statements and other related statements for the financial year ended` IS A DATE
      `the date of dissolution or striking off` IS A DATE
      `the date of the restoration of the name of the company to the register` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344G(2) the company and its directors are not liable to a penalty under section 204 for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the period for filing the financial statements and other related statements for the financial year ended` GREATER THAN `the date of dissolution or striking off` AND `the day on which the period for filing the financial statements and other related statements for the financial year ended` LESS THAN `the date of the restoration of the name of the company to the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "not liable to a penalty under section 204 for a financial year in relation to which the period for filing ... ended (a) after the date of dissolution or striking off; and (b) before the restoration" -- an immunity limited by its own wording; for a financial year whose filing period ended outside those dates the text says nothing

-- src:23104 | (3) On the application by any person, the Court may give such
-- src:23105 | directions and make such orders, as it seems just for placing the
-- src:23106 | company and all other persons in the same position (as nearly as may
-- src:23107 | be) as if the company had not been dissolved or its name had not been
-- src:23108 | struck off the register.
@ref s 344G(3) (src:23104-23108)
GIVEN `a person has applied to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344G(3) the Court may give directions and make orders for placing the company and all other persons in the same position` MEANS
    IF `a person has applied to the Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (ii), fork F-G5): "On the application by any person, the Court may give such directions and make such orders, as it seems just" -- an "On" (upon) gate of a power: "upon" counts as "where" (delegated-definitions ruling (c); periods ruling (b)); the grant ruling's limit 3 lists the site and does not change it

-- src:23112 | (4) An application to the Court for such directions or orders may be
-- src:23113 | made any time within 3 years after the date of restoration of the name
-- src:23114 | of the company to the register.
@ref s 344G(4) (src:23112-23114)
GIVEN `the day on which the application to the Court is made` IS A DATE
      `the date of restoration of the name of the company to the register` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344G(4) the application to the Court is made in time` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the application to the Court is made` AT LEAST `the date of restoration of the name of the company to the register` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of restoration of the name of the company to the register` `the day on which the application to the Court is made` 3 Years
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application to the Court for such directions or orders may be made any time within 3 years after the date of restoration of the name of the company to the register" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); fork F-P5)

-- 344H(1): "Where the name of a company has been struck off and the company dissolved under section 344 or 344A, a person who was an officer of the company immediately before the company was dissolved
-- must ensure that all books and papers of the company are retained for a period of at least 5 years after the date on which the company was dissolved."
-- src:23118 | Retention of books and papers upon striking off
-- src:23120 | 344H.—(1) Where the name of a company has been struck off and
-- src:23121 | the company dissolved under section 344 or 344A, a person who was
-- src:23122 | an officer of the company immediately before the company was
-- src:23123 | dissolved must ensure that all books and papers of the company are
-- src:23124 | retained for a period of at least 5 years after the date on which the
-- src:23125 | company was dissolved.
@ref s 344H(1) (src:23118-23125)
GIVEN `the name of the company has been struck off and the company dissolved under section 344 or 344A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was an officer of the company immediately before the company was dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the company was dissolved` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344H(1) the person must ensure that all the books and papers of the company are retained` MEANS
    IF `the name of the company has been struck off and the company dissolved under section 344 or 344A` AND `the person was an officer of the company immediately before the company was dissolved`
    THEN (IF `the date asked` AT LEAST `the date on which the company was dissolved` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date on which the company was dissolved` `the date asked` 5 Years
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ensure that all books and papers of the company are retained for a period of at least 5 years after the date on which the company was dissolved" (a period the text fixes in its own words; before the dissolution or after the 5 years the periods ruling item (a) gives JUST FALSE; fork F-P5)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; fork F-W1): "Where the name of a company has been struck off and the company dissolved under section 344 or 344A, a person who was an officer of the company immediately before the company was dissolved must ensure" (the "Where" gate of a duty)

-- The duty to retain, as the prohibition it implies (N2 ruling: the text names the bearer): an officer who fails to retain the books and papers within the 5 years breaches it.
-- The trace clock counts days after the date of dissolution (AT 0).
-- src:23118 | Retention of books and papers upon striking off
-- src:23120 | 344H.—(1) Where the name of a company has been struck off and
-- src:23121 | the company dissolved under section 344 or 344A, a person who was
-- src:23122 | an officer of the company immediately before the company was
-- src:23123 | dissolved must ensure that all books and papers of the company are
-- src:23124 | retained for a period of at least 5 years after the date on which the
-- src:23125 | company was dissolved.
@ref s 344H(1) (src:23118-23125)
GIVEN `the name of the officer` IS A STRING
      `the date on which the company was dissolved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 344 act`
`s 344H(1) an officer must not fail to retain the books and papers within 5 years after the dissolution` MEANS
    PARTY Officer `the name of the officer`
    SHANT `s 344H(1) fail to retain all the books and papers of the company`
    WITHIN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date on which the company was dissolved` 5 Years MINUS `the date on which the company was dissolved`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Officer `the name of the officer` BECAUSE "the officer failed to ensure that all books and papers of the company were retained for at least 5 years after the date on which the company was dissolved"

-- src:23129 | (2) An officer of a company who fails to comply with subsection (1)
-- src:23130 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:23131 | not exceeding $2,000.
@ref s 344H(2) (src:23129-23131)
GIVEN `the officer of the company fails to comply with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344H(2) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the officer of the company fails to comply with subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (split site (i), fork F-O1): "An officer of a company who fails to comply with subsection (1) shall be guilty of an offence" -- the element "fails to comply" is unmet

-- src:23129 | (2) An officer of a company who fails to comply with subsection (1)
-- src:23130 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:23131 | not exceeding $2,000.
@ref s 344H(2) (src:23129-23131)
GIVEN `the officer of the company fails to comply with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 344H(2) the most the officer may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 344H(2) the officer of the company is guilty of an offence` `the officer of the company fails to comply with subsection (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 2000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)   -- a fine not exceeding $2,000; no imprisonment; no default penalty
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the officer it makes guilty
